For instance,
for students, the Court often considers the course that they are studying, their academic proficiency,
the family background, etc., to determine and fix what they could earn in the future.

In rural households, they often also assist in the sowing, harvesting and transplanting activities in the field, apart from tending cattle [See Arun Kumar Agrawal (supra);
National Insurance Co. Ltd. v. Minor Deepika rep. by her guardian and next friend, Ranganathan,
2009 SCC OnLine Mad 828].
